preConditionHook:
// RISK TO THE SWING THAT EXISTED WHEN THE TRADE WAS TAKEN, AND LEAVE THE STOP
// THERE. The most recent confirmed swing low is captured on the fill bar and the
// level never moves again; Brooks's stop for limit-order channel entries.
//
// Kept apart from SwingPointTrailingStop, which re-reads the pivot every bar: on
// a trend that runs, the trailed rule exits far higher, and on a trend that never
// prints a new pivot the two are identical. Not StopBeyondExtremeSinceEntry
// either, whose level is a running extreme that WIDENS as the trade goes against
// it, where this one is fixed at entry.
//
// THE LEVEL IS CAPTURED ON ctx.BarsSinceEntry() == 0 -- VERIFIED as 0 on the fill
// bar and as restarting through a reversal, which a ctx.MarketPosition() == 0
// reset would miss because a reversal never passes through flat. It is the same
// at-entry capture convention StopAtSignalBarRangeMultiple and
// PullbackSizedProfitTarget use, and it is what holds "reaches back" at the pivot
// window rather than at the length of the longest trade.
//
// THE PIVOT FORM IS USED, NOT THE lowest-low-over-stopLookback PROXY the source
// offers: the swing primitive is now MEASURED, so the proxy buys nothing.
// stopLookback is therefore the PIVOT WINDOW (EL's Length) rather than a lowest-low
// length -- at the source's 10 with strength 2 the reportable offsets are 2..9.
//
// THE PIVOT SCAN IS INLINED from SwingHigh per the B-list decision, at
// Occurrence 1. MEASURED (EL_Swing_Probe.txt / el_swing_output1.txt, @ES 60 min):
// the pivot test is MIXED -- at-or-beyond the pivotStrength OLDER bars, STRICTLY
// beyond the pivotStrength NEWER bars, and bars-ago indexing makes the SMALLER
// index the NEWER bar, so the strict half is the pk < pj loop; the confirmation
// lag is exactly pivotStrength bars, never 0 or 1, so during the lag the PREVIOUS
// pivot is captured and nothing looks ahead; stopLookback is EL's Length, offsets
// 0..stopLookback-1 inclusive, and the neighbourhood test reaches pivotStrength
// bars PAST the window, so the deepest bar touched is
// stopLookback - 1 + pivotStrength; an empty window returns the -1 SENTINEL, and
// the have-flags are how it is guarded -- a captured -1 as a PRICE sits under
// every real price; the comparisons carry the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance,
// hence el_lt / el_le / el_gt / el_ge. The low side's tie sense is the mirror of
// the measured high-side rule. No WFSafe_SwingLow exists, so plain EL governs.
// Both scans run unconditionally every bar, not only at entry, so Max Bars Back
// covers them and the EasyLanguage call sites advance on the same bars.
//
// Ticks: MinMove/PriceScale are VERIFIED and the tick is written division-first,
// stopTicks * (ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale()), into a local.
//
// Every scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope declaration,
// so the hooks survive a double placement.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
lo1 = -1.0;
for (pj = (int)pivotStrength; pj <= (int)stopLookback - 1; ++pj) {
    pok = true;
    for (pk = pj - (int)pivotStrength; pk < pj; ++pk) {
        if (!el_lt(low[pj], low[pk])) { pok = false; break; }
    }
    if (pok) {
        for (pk = pj + 1; pk <= pj + (int)pivotStrength; ++pk) {
            if (!el_le(low[pj], low[pk])) { pok = false; break; }
        }
    }
    if (pok) { lo1 = low[pj]; break; }
}
hi1 = -1.0;
for (pj = (int)pivotStrength; pj <= (int)stopLookback - 1; ++pj) {
    pok = true;
    for (pk = pj - (int)pivotStrength; pk < pj; ++pk) {
        if (!el_gt(high[pj], high[pk])) { pok = false; break; }
    }
    if (pok) {
        for (pk = pj + 1; pk <= pj + (int)pivotStrength; ++pk) {
            if (!el_ge(high[pj], high[pk])) { pok = false; break; }
        }
    }
    if (pok) { hi1 = high[pj]; break; }
}
if (ctx.BarsSinceEntry() == 0) {
    haveStopLong = el_ne(lo1, -1.0);
    stopLong = lo1;
    haveStopShort = el_ne(hi1, -1.0);
    stopShort = hi1;
}
